# Errors of EXPLAIN (ANALYZE): parsing, statements without a plan, the
# statement's own errors, and errors that running every node to completion
# reveals.

!> EXPLAIN (VERBOSE) SELECT 1
!> EXPLAIN (ANALYZE SELECT 1
!> EXPLAIN (ANALYZE)
!> EXPLAIN ()
!> EXPLAIN (ANALYZE) (ANALYZE) SELECT 1
---
Error: invalid input: expected token ANALYZE, found verbose
Error: invalid input: expected token ), found SELECT
Error: invalid input: unexpected end of input
Error: invalid input: expected token ANALYZE, found )
Error: invalid input: unexpected token (

!> EXPLAIN (ANALYZE) SHOW VIEWS
!> EXPLAIN (ANALYZE) EXPLAIN SELECT 1
!> EXPLAIN (ANALYZE) BEGIN
!> EXPLAIN (ANALYZE) CREATE USER x
!> EXPLAIN (ANALYZE) ANALYZE
!> EXPLAIN (ANALYZE) SELECT $1
!> EXPLAIN (ANALYZE) EXECUTE nosuch
!> DESCRIBE EXPLAIN (ANALYZE) SELECT 1
!> PREPARE p AS EXPLAIN (ANALYZE) SELECT 1
